course: dictionary
lesson: 10022
title: Tender: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «The steak was tender, so it was easy to cut.» A steak you can cut easily is soft, so tender means soft and easy to cut or chew.
explain: «Tender» can also mean gentle and loving. «The closing poem is sad and tender.» A poem cannot be soft to touch, so the word must mean full of gentle, kind feeling.
explain: Ask yourself: what do the other words in the sentence tell me? «A tender bruise» is painful when touched, and «tender loving care» means care that is gentle and kind. Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence and checking that it still makes sense.
explain: Tender can change its job too. As a verb it means to offer something formally, as in «tender your resignation». As a noun, a tender is a formal offer to do a job for a price. Legal tender is money that must be accepted in payment.
fact: «Tender» can mean soft and easy to cut, as in tender meat or tender vegetables.
fact: «Tender» can mean painful when touched, as in a tender bruise.
fact: «Tender» can mean gentle, kind and loving, as in a tender smile.
fact: «Tender» can mean young and not experienced, as in «at a tender age».
fact: «Legal tender» means money that must be accepted in payment.
exercise: «The steak was tender, so it was easy to cut.» What does tender mean here? | Gentle and kind | *Soft and easy to cut | Painful when touched | Young and not experienced
exercise: «The closing poem is sad and tender.» What does tender mean in this sentence? | Old and broken | Hard and cold | Wet and muddy | *Gentle and loving
exercise: Mia says her ankle is tender after she fell. What does tender mean? | Lost in the grass | Easy to cut | *Painful when touched | Very large and swollen like a balloon
test: «Legal tender» is a phrase about money. What does it mean? | *Money that must be accepted in payment | Free sweets from the shop | Coins hidden in a box | Money you can only use on Sundays
test: Dad says, «Tender loving care» helped his plant grow. What does tender loving care mean? | Strict rules and loud shouting | Cutting the plant short | *Care that is gentle and kind | Fast jobs done in a hurry
exam: «She started the job at a tender age.» What does tender mean? | *Young and not experienced | Old and wise | Soft to eat | Painful when touched
